{%- doc -%}
  Outputs the customer's saved product + color pairs as one lookup string:
  `|productId:colorOptionValueId|productId:colorOptionValueId|`. Capture it and test a pair
  with `contains '|<productId>:<optionValueId>|'`. Liquid has no maps, and this keeps each
  lookup a single string test instead of a loop over up to 200 saved pairs.

  @param {object[]} favorites - `customer.metafields.wagner.favorite_colors.value`
    (JSON array of `{"productId": "…", "colorOptionValueId": "…"}`, decimal-string IDs)

  @example
  {%- capture at_favorite_keys -%}{% render 'at-favorite-color-keys', favorites: customer.metafields.wagner.favorite_colors.value %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  echo '|'
  for favorite in favorites
    assign at_pid = favorite.productId | append: '' | strip
    assign at_cid = favorite.colorOptionValueId | append: '' | strip
    if at_pid != blank and at_cid != blank
      echo at_pid | append: ':' | append: at_cid | append: '|'
    endif
  endfor
-%}
